2result.sql is the best match.  
It  
• uses only autosomal chromosomes,  
• filters to common variants (AF ≥ 0.05),  
• keeps only samples that carry ≥1 ALT allele,  
• counts carriers per variant per super‑population and then builds the requested histogram,  
• avoids double‑counting that would arise from joining through `alternate_bases`, and  
• includes all required columns (population size, “is_common_variant”, samples sharing the variant, variant count).

```plaintext
2result.sql
```